The End

10
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
What's going on?

11
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
How is this happening?

12
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Hot springs. Warm water that wells from the center of the earth. They have enchanted humans for ages. People flock from all over to soak their aching bodies in nature's scalding hot baths. Healing, relaxing, and revitalizing. No one can resist their charms.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
NEW THE END

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:06,560
I'm clapping

15
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:15,720
Let's go

16
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:20,620
Wow Wow

17
00:01:45,720 --> 00:02:14,480
Oh, well, I guess that's okay.

18
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,160
It sounds kind of fun, actually.

19
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:20,720
And, I mean, we want the spirits to make discoveries and think for themselves, so I'll make the arrangements.

20
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,720
Besides, we want them happy, right?

21
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:25,020
No one likes an angry spirit.

22
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:25,660
Right.

23
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,540
So, where are you going?

24
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:29,720
I was thinking Tango Paradise.

25
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:30,460
It's its co-ed.

26
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,020
Yes, that's a great one.

27
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,160
Hey, listen, you should join them.

28
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,040
Give yourself a break.

29
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,000
I can take care of everything for you here.

30
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,680
You must think I'm crazy.

31
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:41,100
I absolutely do not.

32
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:44,460
I think you're working too hard, and we can't function if our commander is exhausted.

33
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:45,780
So, do us all a favor.

34
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,040
Go to the hot springs.

35
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,560
What are you really after?

36
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,400
I have no idea what you mean.

37
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:53,180
I have no desire to install several surveillance cameras there.

38
00:02:54,580 --> 00:03:00,800
Would someone like me actually fill a hot spring with lenses so that I could stare at every inch of that hard, tight, young body at my discretion?

39
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,400
Especially the back side.

40
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:07,320
No, no, not the internment camp.

41
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,240
Please have mercy.

42
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,480
Please forgive me, Commander.

43
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,680
Anywhere but there, please.

44
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,380
Listen up, Kanazuki.

45
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,540
When you get to the camp, you're going to start digging a hole and not stop for the entire day.

46
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:22,020
And after that, you'll fill the hole back up and repeat for a whole week.

47
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:28,060
The hot springs with my big brother.

48
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,180
We've had word from headquarters.

49
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:36,300
It's come to my attention that supplementary personnel are currently being deployed from DEM.

50
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,840
And unlike you and your platoon, they've managed to figure out a way to use magic correctly.

51
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:44,880
Not that I think for a moment you would lose to civilian transfers.

52
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:46,160
Far from it.

53
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:49,660
But there's nothing wrong with observing their technique, right?

54
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:52,060
Roger that, sir.

55
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,780
Um, excuse me, Captain.

56
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:01,760
What is it?

57
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:04,060
I wanted to ask about the company trip this weekend.

58
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:09,680
Oh, you mean the 13 Secret Hot Springs Tour with all-you-can-eat delicacies from different regions?

59
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:10,840
Yeah, about that.

60
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:14,660
So you know how more spirits have been turning up lately?

61
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:18,000
Well, our alert levels have increased a tiny bit.

62
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,240
What are you saying?

63
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:25,420
Well, I'm sorry, but the trip has been cancelled.

64
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,980
Screw you spirits!

65
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:30,900
Now hold on.

66
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:32,520
Please, let me finish.

67
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:39,640
I know it won't replace the trip, but the troops and I were thinking, why don't we send you to Tengu Paradise Hot Springs?

68
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,540
You deserve some kind of break.

69
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:44,720
I think a day of relaxation is exactly what you need right now.

70
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,000
It's our way of saying thanks for everything.

71
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:49,520
Plus, it's already handled, so you have to go.

72
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:55,780
Thank you.

73
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:56,720
Very nice work.

74
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:59,060
I think you just earned a double rank position.

75
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:01,760
Okay, but I'm not dead.

76
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:07,220
I can't wait to go.

77
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,140
I love the hot springs.

78
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,760
Best day ever.

79
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:15,400
Listen up!

80
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,260
The captain has accepted our invitation.

81
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,120
Yay!

82
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:21,300
Hot Springs are first!

83
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,020
I do not approve.

84
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:31,720
This is time that you could be using to train and add power to the team.

85
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:32,660
One day?

86
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:42,600
Hello, Shido.

87
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,920
Hey, what's up?

88
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,080
Can I return the book I borrowed from you sometime tomorrow?

89
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:48,720
Of course, that's fine.

90
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:49,680
But why?

91
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,060
Uh, something happened.

92
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,920
Come on, Shido, let's go!

93
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,420
A hot springs paradise of...

94
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:57,240
Okay, you have to stop pulling my shirt.

95
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,260
Sorry, Origami.

96
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,060
I'll talk to you later.

97
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:06,220
Oh, she's mad!

98
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:07,620
Oh, my God, man.

99
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:08,660
She's super mad.

100
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:17,380
Oh, wow.

101
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:18,680
This is so neat.

102
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,240
Hey, that's right.

103
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,480
I forgot this is the first car ride for you two.

104
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:25,440
It's pretty cool, isn't it?

105
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,960
Just be careful not to get car sick.

106
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,120
Oh, pet me, too.

107
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:35,780
Uh, I don't think I can reach that far.

108
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:39,300
It's not fair for you to touch her like that and not me.

109
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:41,100
Come on.

110
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,740
You're the one who said you wanted to sit in the front seat.

111
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,740
Oh, yeah.

112
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:47,680
Look, Shido, I'm in front of you.

113
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:48,960
Pet me, too.

114
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,180
Okay.

115
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:51,680
Who's a cute rat?

116
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,220
Oh, Shido.

117
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:55,980
What's that spinner thing?

118
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:57,620
Oh, that?

119
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:59,080
That's a barber pole.

120
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,440
What about that?

121
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:03,700
I think it's one of those laundry flakes.

122
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:05,380
I don't want that!

123
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:23,760
Okay, if you say so.

124
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:27,220
I never dreamed we would be using the deployment train to take a day trip.

125
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:28,780
Let's not lose track here.

126
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,940
Our goal is to confirm the operation of the vehicle.

127
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:35,900
We're making a periodic check of a route we don't normally use.

128
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:36,740
It's not for fun.

129
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:39,480
So stop messing around and come to order, troops.

130
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,860
She's having fun.

131
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:41,960
She's messing around.

132
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:43,220
Agreed.

133
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,240
The captain's right.

134
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:48,420
If we're going to the hot springs, we need to be well prepared.

135
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,680
We must document this rare outing.

136
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:51,820
Hot springs?

137
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:52,540
Hot springs?

138
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,660
Hot springs?

139
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:03,940
What the hell was that?

140
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,020
I'll check.

141
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,500
What is going on out here?

142
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,760
Oh, really?

143
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:11,880
Okay.

144
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,340
The tunnel caved in, so there's an emergency shutdown.

145
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:17,560
They don't know yet when the service will be restored.

146
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:20,920
Nothing we can do about it now.

147
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:21,580
Troops?

148
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:22,140
Ma'am!

149
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,940
They leave us no choice but to march to our location.

150
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:25,640
Forward!

151
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:26,300
Roger!

152
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:37,180
Will you please forgive me?

153
00:08:39,300 --> 00:08:41,180
That was so cool, Toka!

154
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:43,180
You broke the entire car just by using...

155
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:53,700
Cheer up.

156
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,660
It's going to be okay.

157
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:57,660
Does that mean you're not mad anymore?

158
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,860
No, I'm not mad at all.

159
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:27,460
Several unknowns are turning up on the radar.

160
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:28,920
Confirmation needed.

161
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,480
They have been matched.

162
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:33,520
It's the AST.

163
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:34,660
The AST?

164
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,420
What are they doing here?

165
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:37,760
That's strange.

166
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:39,100
Maybe it's because of the spirits?

167
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,400
I highly doubt it.

168
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:43,620
They aren't even able to detect spirit waves from Toka and the others right now.

169
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,820
Don't worry about why.

170
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:47,940
Any contact we make now could interfere with the plan.

171
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:49,760
Sound the emergency code.

172
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:50,680
We should wait.

173
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,340
The commander's out on business.

174
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:55,240
And our second-in-command is busy with this punishment.

175
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:55,840
Enough!

176
00:09:55,840 --> 00:10:01,680
According to Article 22, Clause 3, if there's an emergency, we have the right to transfer command.

177
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:05,540
If at least five crew members agree, we can sound the code.

178
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,780
Jove, hands on sounding the code!

179
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,000
Confirmed!

180
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,680
I bet Marriage Kawagaway temporarily accept the role of deputy commander.

181
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,260
Yes, deputy commander.

182
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:23,220
I like the sound of that.

183
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:24,980
Activate the code!

184
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,240
Form the absolute defense line!

185
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,720
And prepare to attack!

186
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,440
Block the advance of the AST!

187
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,060
Roger!

188
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:44,200
Yep, I was right.

189
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:45,720
This is much different from the map.

190
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,460
That street doesn't look familiar.

191
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:48,880
Captain!

192
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,700
There's a dead end up ahead!

193
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,540
The right flank is also a dead end!

194
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,440
There's a shopping arcade 500 miles straight ahead of us!

195
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,460
Behind us!

196
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:57,760
The street has been destroyed!

197
00:10:58,660 --> 00:10:59,960
We can't help that.

198
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,840
Hey, Origami.

199
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:01,400
Ma'am.

200
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:02,780
Keep watch from up above.

201
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:03,700
Roger that.

202
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:09,720
Checking.

203
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:14,620
There is no shopping arcade over to the left, but I do see a side road a short distance ahead.

204
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,820
Looks like it connects to the main road after about a quarter of a mile.

205
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:18,800
That'll work!

206
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,720
Troops, forward, march!

207
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:34,660
What do you want to do?

208
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:35,660
It's so good to see you!

209
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:37,660
Hello? Is there something wrong?

210
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:39,660
No, not at all. I was just...

211
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:42,660
I wanted to make sure that Shida was doing his job.

212
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,660
What? You can do all that from the ship.

213
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,660
Be real, you just wanted to come with us to the hot springs, right?

214
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:49,660
Don't be ridiculous.

215
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:53,660
Look, it's okay. Why don't we all go together? It'll be a lot of fun.

216
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:56,660
Well, I guess if you insist. Let's go!

217
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:03,660
What in the world is going on?

218
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:05,660
So, if you need anything, just let me know, okay?

219
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:07,660
Thanks, I guess, but what about you?

220
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:09,660
I said I'm fine! Gah!

221
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,660
I'll catch up with you later.

222
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:11,660
Okay.

223
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:14,660
Oh, man. Why did something have to happen now?

224
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:17,660
This is starting to get ridiculous!

225
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:20,660
There was definitely a path plot here.

226
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:24,660
No reaction here. Vibration and infrared sensor failed.

227
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:27,660
No reaction from the acoustic sensor either.

228
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:30,660
And no humans detected within 500 meters.

229
00:12:30,660 --> 00:12:33,660
The walls around here are a minimum of 50 centimeters thick

230
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:35,660
and are heavily enforced with rebar.

231
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:40,660
Like that'll stop me!

232
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:42,660
Bring it here.

233
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:43,660
Right.

234
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:44,660
Whoop!

235
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:45,660
Whoop!

236
00:12:45,660 --> 00:12:46,660
Whoop!

237
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:47,660
Whoop!

238
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:48,660
Whoop!

239
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:49,660
Whoop!

240
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,660
Whoop!

241
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:51,660
Whoop!

242
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:52,660
What just happened here!

243
00:12:52,660 --> 00:13:01,100
What just happened here?

244
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:02,240
Uh-oh, what's that?

245
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:03,880
Did I do something just now?

246
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:05,220
No, you did nothing.

247
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,260
The wall exploded all by itself.

248
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:10,020
Oh, no, that's so scary!

249
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:11,480
Crap.

250
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,640
It figures.

251
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:15,460
Looks like the damn AST decided to meddle again.

252
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,780
Switch to Datetown Type 2 in combat mode.

253
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:22,140
And use whatever firearms you feel are necessary.

254
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:24,120
Commander? What are you doing out there?

255
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:27,520
The site inspection. Don't worry about me. Confirm your orders.

256
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:31,660
Right. Transitioning to Datetown Type 2 in combat mode.

257
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,120
Eliminating the AST.

258
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:46,660
What is this?

259
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:52,160
Rose! What's it happening?

260
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:56,180
Move carefully. This doesn't feel right.

261
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,120
Look alive, ladies. And hurry!

262
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:18,280
The commander is watching. Do whatever it takes to stop them.

263
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:18,780
Roger!

264
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:26,740
What's this?

265
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,660
A mobility inhibition system.

266
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,260
It spills a special liquid on the ground to lower friction coefficient to below .01.

267
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:35,460
Meant to prevent the progression of the target.

268
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,240
Damn. What about the one over there?

269
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:45,300
Probably some kind of hypnotic gas. Helpful for when the enemy wants to stop us without killing us.

270
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:47,340
Well played, whoever you are.

271
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:50,300
Listen up! Use the suppression equipment!

272
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:52,440
Attack immediately!

273
00:14:52,440 --> 00:15:22,420
Attack immediately!

